  "confidence": "datasheet",
  "source": "Raspberry Pi 5 mechanical drawing (Raspberry Pi Ltd, 1:1 at A4), with positions read from its vector geometry: board 85 x 56 mm with 3 mm corners, four 2.7 mm holes on a 58 x 49 mm pattern, 40-pin header centred 32.5 mm along the top hole line. Bottom edge: USB-C at 11.2 mm, micro HDMI at 25.8 and 39.2 mm. Right edge: Ethernet centred 10.2 mm and standing 3 mm past the board, USB 3.0 pair at 29.1 mm, USB 2.0 pair at 47 mm, so the layout is not the Pi 4 one. Power button 18.4 mm up the left edge, sticking out 0.45 mm. Heights from the side view: USB-C 3.2, micro HDMI 3.4, UART connector 4.4, camera/display connectors 4.1 mm; the USB and Ethernet heights are the Pi 4 parts. The two 3 mm holes for the Active Cooler push pins are not mounting holes and are left out.",
